<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/apion-family"><span class="enc-name">Apion family</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Apion family were a dynasty of great landowners in Byzantine Egypt, based at Oxyrhynchus, from the fifth to the early seventh century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/apis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/apis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Apis</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Apis was a sacred bull worshipped at Memphis in ancient Egypt as the living manifestation of the god Ptah.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/apolinario-mabini"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/apolinario-mabini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Apolinario Mabini</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Apolinario Mabini was a Filipino lawyer and political thinker who became the chief adviser of Emilio Aguinaldo in 1898, despite being paralysed.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/apollo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/apollo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Apollo</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Apollo is a major god of Greek and Roman religion, son of Zeus and Leto and twin brother of Artemis.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/apollo-delphinios"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/apollo-delphinios.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Apollo Delphinios</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Apollo Delphinios was a form of the Greek god Apollo, linked to dolphins, the sea and the founding of colonies.</span></a></li><l