-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arabia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arabia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Arabia is the region of the Arabian Peninsula in south-west Asia, bounded by the Red Sea, the Arabian Sea and the Persian Gulf.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arabia-felix"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arabia-felix.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arabia Felix</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Arabia Felix ('Fortunate Arabia') was the Greek and Roman name for the south-west of the Arabian Peninsula, roughly modern Yemen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arabia-petraea"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arabia-petraea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arabia Petraea</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Arabia Petraea was a province of the Roman Empire formed in 106 CE when Trajan annexed the Nabataean kingdom.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/arabian-peninsula"><span class="enc-name">Arabian Peninsula</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arabian Peninsula is the large peninsula of south-west Asia between the Red Sea and the Persian Gulf.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arabian-sea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arabian Sea</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arabian Sea is the part of the northern Indian Ocean between Arabia and the Indian subcontinent.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/arabic-language"><span class="enc-name">Arabic language</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Arabic is a Semitic language that spread with Islam from the Arabian Peninsula across the Middle East and North Africa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arabisation"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arabisation.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arabisation</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">Arabisation refers to the policy, begun under the Umayyad caliph Abd al-Malik in the 690s, of making Arabic the official language of administration.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/arabs"><span class="enc-name">Arabs</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arabs are a people originating in the Arabian Peninsula who speak Arabic.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/arabshahid-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Arabshahid dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arabshahids were a Chinggisid dynasty descended from Shiban that ruled Khwarazm, the Khanate of Khiva, from 1511.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arab–Byzantine wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 629–1050s</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arab–Byzantine wars were fought between the Byzantine Empire and the Arab caliphates and their successor emirates from 629 into the 11th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arab-khazar-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arab-khazar-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arab–Khazar wars</span><span class="enc-type">War</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arab–Khazar wars were a series of conflicts in the seventh and eighth centuries between the Khazar Khaganate and the Umayyad and early Abbasid caliphates over…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arachosia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arachosia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arachosia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Arachosia was an ancient region in present-day southern Afghanistan, centred around Kandahar.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arachthos"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arachthos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arachthos</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arachthos is a river of Epirus in north-western Greece, flowing from the Pindus mountains south past Arta into the Ambracian Gulf.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arad-romania"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arad-romania.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arad, Romania</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Arad is a city in western Romania on the Mureș river, part of the Kingdom of Hungary until 1920.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arade"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arade</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arade is a river of the western Algarve in southern Portugal, flowing past Silves to the Atlantic at Portimão.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/arado-flugzeugwerke"><span class="enc-name">Arado Flugzeugwerke</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">Arado Flugzeugwerke was a German aircraft maker founded in 1925 at Warnemünde near Rostock.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arae-flaviae